/-!
# Symplectic-four diagram automorphisms and local extension cores

Diagram preservation refers to the conjugacy classes of the actual point
and plane parabolics. Semilinear classification proves that binary
diagram-preserving automorphisms are inner, so faithful normal binary
extensions preserving the diagram have no proper overgroup. For nonbinary
fields, the actual local SL₂ actions retain their faithful field contribution.
Their two-element kernels give equality of the embedded local two-core with
the core of its join with a normalizing subgroup. Normality is proved inside
that local join, and both cores are compared in the same ambient group.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, F.1.12, printed pp.263--264 of `refs/quasithin.pdf`.
-/
